    "explanation": "Both parties largely agree on the routing facts; the live question is the ERP. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00103, weight 1.0 — 100% coverage, 10 s sampling, maximum gap 0 s, so no limb of POL-RD-07 is engaged) measures the trip at 11.18 km against a booked optimal of 8.2 km (EV-TRIP-00103), an excess of 2.98 km, or 36.34% of optimal. That clears both limbs of POL-RD-01, so a deviation is ESTABLISHED, but it is not material (below 50% and below 8.0 km).\n\nThat deviation is fully exonerated under POL-RD-03. The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-00103-01 names Braddell Road, the arterial the platform's own optimal route uses ('Braddell Rd -> Serangoon Rd -> Kallang arterials, no gantry'); its 05:30–12:00 window covers the trip window with 35.2 minutes to spare (well beyond the 15-minute buffers); and the trace leaves the corridor at the Lorong 1 Toa Payoh slip and rejoins after. The exoneration cap is min(measured 2.98 km, 1.30 x (10.6 - 8.2) + 1.00 = 4.12 km) = 2.98 km, so the whole measured excess is justified. The closure-adjusted optimal is 8.2 + 2.98 = 11.18 km, exactly the trace distance, leaving no unexonerated excess.\n\nBecause POL-RD-03 excuses the excess in full, POL-RD-02 does not run and the distance and time charges stand: base 3.80, distance 8.40, time 8.12, platform fee 0.80, plus the contested pass-throughs. The driver's alternative arithmetic (charged_total 25.12 against a closure-adjusted recomputed fare of 20.99, a difference of 4.127 rounding to 4.15) and the rider's mirror claim for 4.15 are both put aside: a POL-RD-02 recomputation against the adjusted route applies only to excess beyond the POL-RD-03 cap, and there is none. POL-RD-09(1) would in any event forbid adding the off-route ERP on top of a POL-RD-02 figure.\n\nWhat does move is the ERP. The optimal route crosses no gantry (optimal_route_erp_sgd 0.00), yet the rider was charged 4.00 across two CTE gantries, both flagged on_optimal_route false: CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) 3.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd towards City) 1.00. Where a deviation is exonerated as an external event under POL-RD-03, POL-RD-09(2) refunds off-route ERP to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction, capped at 12.00. The 4.00 is under the cap and is refunded in full.\n\nThe driver's argument that no ERP refund is due because the detour was rider-caused under POL-RD-09(3) is rejected. POL-RD-04 requires a rider instruction that identifies a place or road specifically enough to act on. The only routing message is the driver's own 'braddell close today, i take CTE ah'; the rider's 'ok' is bare acknowledgement and names no place or route, and both messages carry waypoint_hint null, so there is no rider waypoint to corroborate. POL-RD-04 is therefore unavailable and its corroboration test cannot be run; POL-RD-09(3) is not engaged and does not bar the pass-through correction.\n\nNo referral arises. Both gantries are matched to the trace under POL-RD-09's own 250 m test (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 40.25 m), so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 553 completed trips in 90 days, neither limb of POL-RD-06 is met and the deviation is not material, so no POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral. All artifacts relied on carry weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and the ruling rests well above the 0.70 floor. The rider's claim is allowed to the extent of the 4.00 ERP and no further: 4.00 is refunded, the rest of the charge stands."
